//---- LEADER-AGE
A recurring theme among world leaders. But Trump and Putin are not the oldest men leading their nations. How exceptional is it to hold the highest office when well over the retirement age?



//---- NOSOP3-CLIMATECHANGE

<a href='https://youtu.be/xRLbCYK_7fc?si=7SAsK9MpXpFLdqP_' target='_blank'>This video</a> explains the complexity of climate change by looking into the past, present and future.

I translated the script visually into a metaphor of a rubik’s cube to depict this complicity: changing one factor affects the others. I designed both the physical cubes in the set and the motion graphics that animate the story, creating a visual language that makes the interconnections tangible and understandable. 


//---- DEMO-IRAN
In late 2025, widespread protests erupted in Iran over rising oil prices and growing dissatisfaction, only to be violently suppressed while the government cut off internet access, leaving video and information scarce. 

<a href='https://youtu.be/5gw0s13itnA?si=fuW28PBg2_-4kMI9' target='_blank'>This project</a> started with a dataset of verified protest videos, each tagged by incident type and location. My role was to translate that data into a series of maps and a timeline. I used tags to plot separate maps showing different types of incidents, and selecting which videos to surface to show that demonstrations were spreading across the country rather than concentrated in one place.


//---- COALITION
After the Dutch general elections in 2021, multiple parties needed to negotiate a coalition with at least 76 of 150 seats. 

I translated the complex political process visually into a metaphor of a strategic board game, representing each party with a number of pawns reflecting their seats. By combining motion graphics with tangible objects, I contributed to this video to show the possible coalition scenarios clear and accessible for a younger audience.

//---- CHININDREST
'Meer dan babipangang' founder Julie Ng worked on a documentary about the heritage of Chin. Ind. Rest.: Chinese Indonesian restaurants, a well known formula for restaurants in the Netherlands. As a daughter of a former owner of such restaurant, she also dug into her personal history.

<a href='https://bersamamagazine.nl/' target='_blank'>Bersama magazine</a> launched a special edition with recipes from Julie's dad, straight from the Chin. Ind. Rest. kitchen. I illustrated over 30 dishes, all well familiar from my own time working in a Chin. Ind. Rest. from the age of 16-19. 



//---- PORTRAITS
Within the Dutch Ministry of Justice and Security in The Hague meeting rooms are named after Dutch artists and thinkers. 

Each of these 14 meeting rooms are now provided with illustrated portraits reflected on what made them stand out, how their work moved our science, art, philosophy or social environment forward throughout history.


//---- uitgezocht
I created the visual style of a newly launched Youtube explainer format called ‘Uitgezocht’, part of NOS jeugdjournaal: news for children aged 8-12 years old. 

The visual style had to fit within the existing identity of NOS Jeugdjournaal but also needed to have it’s own identity. Using simple geometric forms animated in a light, bouncy way, I developed a look that is playful for children but adaptable to more serious topics. 

I also designed the animated bumper that introduces each explainer and briefly presents the topic, ensuring a cohesive and engaging visual identity across episodes.